LWAYS provide a fallback path when retrieval is on the critical path — silent failure of external sources produces vacuous downstream output. Naturally composes into research-then-synthesize shells (sequential research → synthesis), briefing-generation (with structured per-source output), and fallback-recovery shells (primary source + backup). Avoid when all material is already in :reads or the task is purely structural.\n\nCAPABILITIES:\n- formulate one or more search/retrieval queries from the task goal, fan out queries, collect raw source material into a named :writes key\n- natural fit at the start of a tree when the task needs evidence the model doesn't already have in context\n- outputs are typically a vector of source snippets or a map of source-id → raw content for downstream extraction/synthesis\n\nREPRESENTATIVE USES:\n- pre-analysis fact gathering: 'find recent rulings on X' → top-N case snippets with citations\n- pre-synthesis briefing: 'collect what's known about company Y' → multi-source dossier\n- pre-classification grounding: 'lookup definitions of these terms' → controlled-vocabulary anchors"} {:granularity :tree-fingerprint, :target-id #uuid "9880798a-8487-3a24-93e4-b59c5ae5d789", :body {:capabilities ["given a symbol to rename or relocate, change its definition and EVERY reference across the codebase (including tests) while preserving behavior exactly" "natural fit when the task is a pure refactor of identity — rename calc -> compute-tax everywhere, move a fn to another namespace — with zero behavior change" "outputs are typically a set of coordinated edits across all referencing files + evidence that no call site was missed and behavior is unchanged"], :strengths [{:trait "ENUMERATE every reference before editing — find all call sites (definition, callers, tests, docs) so the rename/move is exhaustive; a missed reference is a compile/runtime break", :good-when "the symbol is referenced from multiple files including tests", :recommended-pattern "[:sequence [:code {:reads [:symbol :repo] :writes [:references] :fn (fn [{:keys [inputs]}] {:references :all-call-sites})}] [:map-each {:items :references :as :ref :writes [:edits]} [:llm {:reads [:ref :new-name] :writes [:edit]}]] [:final {:keys [:edits]}]]", :confidence 0.7, :evidence-count 1} {:trait "gate the change on a compile/test run after editing — a behavior-preserving rename/move is correct ONLY if everything still resolves and the existing tests stay green", :good-when "a build or test command exists to confirm exhaustiveness and behavior preservation", :recommended-pattern "[:sequence [:llm {:writes [:edits]}] [:code {:reads [:edits] :writes [:build-result] :fn (fn [{:keys [inputs]}] {:build-result :compiles-tests-green})}] [:final {:keys [:edits :build-result]}]]", :confidence 0.7, :evidence-count 1}], :avoid-when ["the task changes behavior or adds functionality — that is code-building, not a behavior-preserving rename/move" "the change is a data reshape rather than an identity refactor of code symbols — that is the Transformation behavior" "the task is to extract a helper, pull out a function, or otherwise refactor/restructure code — that is code-building/refactor, NOT a pure identity rename or move of an existing symbol"], :weaknesses [{:trait "editing only the definition and the obvious callers (a code-building instinct that stops at the first file) leaves stale references in tests/docs/secondary namespaces — the rename is half-applied and the build breaks", :avoid-when "the symbol is referenced beyond the file that defines it", :recommended-alternative "first enumerate ALL references repo-wide (grep/AST), then map-each an edit over every site, then compile to confirm none was missed", :confidence 0.7, :evidence-count 1} {:trait "sneaking a behavior change into a rename/move (renaming AND tweaking logic) destroys the refactor's safety — reviewers can no longer trust it as a no-op and regressions hide in the diff", :avoid-when "the task is strictly a