ved behavioral subtrees for task planning and tool-chain orchestration" "Evaluating tree-class candidates for code generation or execution workflows" "Filtering out irrelevant retrieved documents based on strict domain and constraint matching" "Auditing candidate metadata quality by observing how avoid-when guards trigger" "Validating structural alignment of tool-chain workflows (e.g., edit-apply-verify loops)"], :version 18, :consolidated-from-event-count 350}, :expected-signature "TREE SUMMARY:\nThis node functions as an LLM-powered candidate reranker that evaluates retrieved behavioral subtrees or tree classes against specific user tasks, producing a structured JSON array of candidates annotated with fitness scores and highly detailed, quote-backed reasoning. It excels at identifying deep structural workflow matches (such as tool-chain sequences, emitted worked-DSL patterns, and verification loops) and strictly enforcing negative constraints (avoid-when guards), sharply down-ranking candidates that violate these conditions. While highly effective for complex task-to-tool matching, it is overly penalizing when candidate metadata contains contradictory or flawed avoid-when clauses (e.g., an edit-apply-verify subtree guarding against actual file changes), effectively blinding it to perfect structural matches due to its strict adherence to hard-rule guard penalties. Additionally, its deep reasoning process introduces significant latency for batch evaluations, and it occasionally wraps JSON outputs in markdown code fences, making pre-filtering and deterministic post-processing advisable for production pipelines.\n\nCAPABILITIES:\n- Evaluates and scores retrieved behavioral-subtree and tree-class candidates against complex user intents\n- Generates detailed, quote-backed reasoning that maps candidate metadata to task requirements\n- Outputs structured JSON arrays of ranked candidates with fitness scores\n- Strictly enforces candidate avoid-when guards, applying sharp penalties for metadata conflicts\n- Distinguishes deep structural workflow fits (e.g., tool-chain sequences, emitted worked-DSL) from superficial keyword matches\n- Synthesizes multi-step toolchain requirements (e.g., read -> edit -> verify)\n- Detects and penalizes metadata contradictions (e.g., flawed avoid-when clauses that contradict the candidate's primary purpose)\n\nREPRESENTATIVE USES:\n- Ranking retrieved behavioral subtrees for task planning and tool-chain orchestration\n- Evaluating tree-class candidates for code generation or execution workflows\n- Filtering out irrelevant retrieved documents based on strict domain and constraint matching\n- Auditing candidate metadata quality by observing how avoid-when guards trigger\n- Validating structural alignment of tool-chain workflows (e.g., edit-apply-verify loops)"} {:granularity :node-instance, :target-id [#uuid "430e533d-caed-5d3f-9048-dd2c3e6e48f7" #uuid "8b9dc33d-b97f-51d3-bf0f-1eb8c09bf97c"], :body {:capabilities ["reads workspace files via fs/read or code-read" "modifies file contents using LLM or inline string manipulation" "writes files via fs/write or gated code-write" "verifies behavioral changes via shell/exec or code-shell" "emits behavior trees to sequence gated workspace operations"], :strengths [{:trait "recovers from blocking conditions by switching to emit-tree!", :good-when "initial inline mutation attempts fail with orc blocking condition", :recommended-pattern "route all workspace mutations through gated catalog functions inside an emitted sequence tree", :confidence 0.9, :evidence-count 8, :first-observed-at "2026-07-31T15:42:40Z", :last-reinforced-at "2026-07-31T17:55:03Z"}], :avoid-when ["using raw mutating tools directly in Phase-1 REPL without emit-tree!" "relying on LLM to output raw code without fence-stripping safeguards"], :weaknesses [{:trait "triggers orc blocking condition with inline mutating tools", :avoid-when "executing fs/write or shell/exec directly in Phase-1 REPL", :recom