e mutation routing", :good-when "Performing file edits that require user approval and proper tool-context threading.", :recommended-pattern "Use `emit-tree!` with `code-write` and `code-shell` catalog functions to safely route mutations and trigger permission prompts.", :confidence 0.95, :evidence-count 12, :first-observed-at "2026-07-31T15:53:06Z", :last-reinforced-at "2026-07-31T17:55:03Z"} {:trait "Grounded read-write-verify orchestration", :good-when "The task requires modifying workspace files and proving the change works via execution rather than just generating code.", :recommended-pattern "Enforce a strict sequence of code-write followed by code-shell, ensuring the final response reads from both results to prevent pure-design responses.", :confidence 0.9, :evidence-count 20, :first-observed-at "2026-07-31T10:48:46Z", :last-reinforced-at "2026-07-31T13:04:14Z"}], :avoid-when ["Candidate metadata contains contradictory avoid-when guards that falsely trigger" "Strict low-latency or low-token-budget requirements apply to large batch evaluations" "Executing raw inline workspace mutations without gated catalog wrappers" "Relying on LLM to output large, raw file contents without robust parsing fallbacks" "The downstream LLM leaf generating verification commands is prone to hallucinating blank inputs"], :weaknesses [{:trait "Vulnerability to contradictory candidate metadata", :avoid-when "Candidate documents contain flawed, overly broad, or contradictory avoid-when clauses that conflict with their primary purpose.", :recommended-alternative "Fix the candidate's avoid-when metadata at the source, or use a more forgiving scoring function that weighs structural fit higher than literal guard matches.", :confidence 0.95, :evidence-count 40, :first-observed-at "2026-07-31T15:54:26Z", :last-reinforced-at "2026-07-31T17:50:46Z"} {:trait "High latency and token cost on batch evaluations", :avoid-when "Real-time or low-latency response is required for large candidate sets (>1