valuating retrieved behavioral subtrees against user tasks, generating comprehensive reasoning, and strictly enforcing negative constraints (avoid-when guards), though it suffers from high latency on large batches and can be overly penalized by contradictory metadata. As a workspace orchestrator, it manages read-edit-verify workflows, demonstrating strong self-correction by falling back to deterministic string manipulation when LLM generation fails, and successfully routing mutations through gated `emit-tree!` catalog functions. However, it frequently triggers sandbox violations when attempting raw inline mutations and struggles with LLM full-file generation fragility, markdown fence contamination, and skipped verification steps. To use this node reliably, ensure candidate metadata is clean, pre-filter large reranking batches, and strictly route all file mutations through gated catalog wrappers with validated verification commands.", :representative-uses ["Ranking retrieved behavioral subtrees and tree-classes for task planning" "Single-file code modification and behavioral verification via CLI" "Filtering out irrelevant retrieved documents based on strict domain constraints" "Iterative recovery from LLM formatting failures using inline string replacement"], :version 1, :consolidated-from-event-count 10}, :expected-signature "TREE SUMMARY:\nThis node instance operates as a versatile LLM execution engine, primarily observed performing two distinct roles: semantic candidate reranking and workspace file manipulation. As a reranker, it excels at evaluating retrieved behavioral subtrees against user tasks, generating comprehensive reasoning, and strictly enforcing negative constraints (avoid-when guards), though it suffers from high latency on large batches and can be overly penalized by contradictory metadata. As a workspace orchestrator, it manages read-edit-verify workflows, demonstrating strong self-correction by falling back to deterministic string manipulation when